WEBVTT

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.380
Unexplained cases of human combustion
 all over the world...

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.480
...World Health Organization 
is investigating spontaneous combustion...

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.380
<i>Burnish, a sudden mutation...</i>

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.200
Governments of all countries 
take action to stop Burnish

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.200
<i>...that is thought to cause self-combustion...</i>

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.670
Segregation policies are being implemented...

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.830
Radical group Mad Burnish's...

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.170
...terrorist blaze attacks on the rise.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.230
UN-appointed specialist Prof. Prometh

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.130
said that oppression of the Burnish may lead to
concurrent blazes worldwide.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.700
The Great World Blaze has come to an end...

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.030
...50% of the global population suffers...

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.400
...30 years after the Great World Blaze,

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.580
now more than ever we must strive to keep peace.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.960
<i>Fire in high-rise building.</i>

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>Area B-25,
Promepolis New Town Center.</i>

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.590
<i>Dispatch request for Burning Rescue.</i>

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.470
<i>Dispatch request for Burning Rescue.</i>

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.890
Burning Rescue!

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.180
Dispatch!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.700
- It's a Burnish Flare! 
 - Where's Burning Rescue?

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.550
The automatic extinguishers have failed!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.200
<i>We can't cope!</i>

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.120
<i>We're doomed!</i>

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.620
Yeah, yeah. We're almost there.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.670
Many people on the 58th floor!

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.840
Looks like the center of the Burnish blaze!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.510
Varys! Remi!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.650
<i>Emergency deployment 
with anti-Burnish combat equipment.</i>

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:51.700
OK.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.350
Roger.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:59.750
Lucia! Launch while in motion as soon 
as we get in range.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.730
GO!

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.310
On the scene.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.600
It's full of Burnish Flares here.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.770
Quick, Remi!

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.350
Here they are!

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.020
You're safe now.
Keep calm.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:25.480
The ceiling...!

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.230
I got it.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.860
Let's get out while we can.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.580
Everyone in the container.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.590
Rescuemobile on the scene.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.010
Aina! How's it going?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:57.180
58th floor rescue complete.
In transit.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.690
<i>There are people on the roof.</i>

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.810
Burnish lightning!
Instrument malfunction.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.320
Can't get any closer.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.570
Launch Galo!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.210
Woah. It's burning hard.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.050
Well worth extinguishing.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.720
It sets my firefighter's soul on fire!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:44.230
Sorry for the wait. Burning Rescue's here!

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.350
Breath ease, folks! The amazing
Galo is on the scene!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.520
Stop messing around, Galo.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.270
We'll launch you to the 108th floor.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.490
I'm not messing around.
I'm jazzing up the place.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.860
Stop talking nonsense.
You'll bite your tongue.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:58.950
Launch!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.780
Never fear, Galo is...

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.260
Look! Rescue's here.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.840
Where are they going?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:28.940
He's dead.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.310
Must be dead.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.530
I'm alive!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.990
Come on, this way.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.740
Galo, get rid of the smoke already!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.180
Come on, this way.
Get on.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.810
<i>Galo! Behind you.</i>

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.730
<i>Strong Burnish signals coming from behind the smoke.</i>

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.860
<i>They're growing stronger!</i>

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.680
Captain. It's Mad Burnish!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.220
The flame terrorists?

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.640
Yes. Most have been arrested,

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.180
but the leader and
two top brass were on the run.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.640
Galo, listen.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.900
Mankind's been after him for 30 years.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.360
He's the instigator of Burnish crimes.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.150
Mad Burnish's leader.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.820
<i>Your rescue gear will do no good.</i>

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:00.950
<i>Wait for help.</i>

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.660
So, that's the boss.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:03.910
<i>Galo!</i>

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.780
Aina. Rescue has priority. Go, quick!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.500
<i>Don't do anything crazy.</i>

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.250
Like he's gonna listen.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.250
You're damn right.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
A little burn never scared a firefighter.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:21.090
You'll find me dead before letting
 those firebugs loose.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.630
You, fireball bastards!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.550
Hey!

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.780
Is that it? You're all talk.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.660
Fireboy.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.030
Rescue gear's too heavy to compete with bikes.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.990
They're too fast.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.290
<i>Pull that thing out then, Lucia.</i>

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.120
Righto.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.460
<i>It's tuned and ready. Can load at any time.</i>

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.040
Go!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.750
Tech on!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.600
Though the fire is gone,
the heart is tempered.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.110
I'll put you out with my burning soul!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.070
Click.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.250
Be amazed! Matoi embodies the heritage

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.040
of a Far East island's firefighter.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.630
It symbolizes the spirit of the men

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.170
who fought fire with their bare hands.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:47.680
<i>I won't let you do what you want forever, 
firebug bastards!</i>

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:48.640
Is he stupid?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:49.470
He is stupid.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.140
You fool!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.480
How the hell!?

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.490
Here's one.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.700
Gueira! What?!

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.670
And two.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.000
Come down, big boss!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.600
Get off your high horse...

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:30.680
And fight me! One-on-one!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.360
Shit.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.280
Coward! Attacking me when I was
 striking a pose.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.000
Only an idiot poses while firefighting!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.620
Lucia!
What the hell is that toy?

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.880
From an idea I had. Sorry.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.550
<i>Galo, don't get too excited.
Stay calm.</i>

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.840
I'm always calm.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:15.010
Hey! Are you messing with me?

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.440
<i>Here he goes again.</i>

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.060
Interesting.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.400
One-on-one!

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.690
What's fun about
burning people's houses?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.250
It's not our choice.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.850
The flames are part of us.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.500
We must burn in order to live.
That's the way we Burnish are.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.040
Only your soul should burn.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.920
Your flames are a nuisance.
I'll put 'em out.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:32.340
With my burning soul.
That's my style.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.930
You're talking nonsense.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.140
Shut up!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.150
Heave-ho.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:27.650
<i>Idiot.</i>

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.830
You're just a kid.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.000
Look who's talking.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.150
Get out of my way or die.

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:56.130
We Burnish don't kill without reason.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.800
You have nothing to protect yourself.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.000
You're naked.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.520
Don't you act big, firebug bastard!

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.810
I'm...
No, actually, <i>we're</i>...

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.860
a rescue team.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:31.590
Lucia!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.550
You got it!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:43.930
How do you like it?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.390
Matoi Tech rapid cooling.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.100
This is Special Mobile Firefighter Rescue Unit

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:57.030
Burning Rescue's teamwork.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:03.280
Are you in awe now? 
I didn't get naked for fun.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.370
It didn't cross my mind.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.620
The name is Galo Thymos.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:11.880
A firefighter with a burning soul.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.750
Remember that, Leader of the Mad Burnish!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.650
My name is Lio.
Lio Fotia.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:29.140
You're too cocky, rookie.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.770
Ow!

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:34.360
<i>Jeez. The suit was brand new;
would it kill you to be more careful?</i>

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.850
You can get better data that way.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.150
You went overboard, idiot.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.700
You hit me too hard, Varys!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.070
Hit him even harder,

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.240
otherwise this idiot won't learn.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.870
Aina, you...

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.620
Freeze Force.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.050
Colonel Vulcan.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.350
Good job, Ignis.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:15.020
We'll take the Mad Burnish.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:22.860
Hey, you're working hard
with this old gear.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.990
Life must be hard for
a low-level rescue team.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:31.870
But, Burnish crimes are under
Freeze Force's jurisdiction.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.460
Taking credit for our work.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:34.790
Hey, stop it!

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.750
Was it you who caught him?

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:47.640
What if I was?

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.640
You've exceeded your authority.
I'm arresting you.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.640
What?

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.560
The law forbids civilians
from dealing with terrorists.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.650
You could've caused
a major disaster.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.530
I can't overlook
your reckless actions.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.070
It's the Burnish's crimes
that can't be overlooked.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.990
I've only stopped them.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.740
Make your objections in court.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.200
Wait.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:14.040
We're authorized to deal with
them in case of a fire emergency.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.290
That should apply.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:20.420
The right to decide is mine.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.170
Is this a legitimate decisions?

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.770
You can't take a joke.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:39.480
Internal power struggle?
Public officials are so petty.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:45.530
How dare you, Burnish?
Take him away!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:57.830
Looks like Vulcan
was taking it out on you.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.330
Huh?

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:14.100
<i>The Burnish suddenly appeared 30 years ago.</i>

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:18.770
<i>Large fires caused by fire-handling mutants</i>

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:21.150
<i>took a big toll on the world.</i>

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:25.900
<i>But, now the Burnish threat's being driven out.</i>

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>The other day, thanks to Burning Rescue's intervention,</i>

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:35.750
<i>Mad Burnish's leader was arrested.</i>

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:40.290
<i>This marks the end of the flame terrorist group.</i>

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:49.550
Ouch.

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:50.930
Ow!

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.140
Wait!

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:57.810
He said wait! Damn!

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:02.770
It's useless.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:06.400
You'll only get frozen limbs.

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:08.030
Looks like it.

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:09.110
Boss.

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:18.000
This is...

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.290
It's terrible.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:21.000
It's just like they said.

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:25.460
You were our only hope,
but now you've got caught too.

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:28.880
Boss.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:40.560
What have we done
to deserve this?

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:45.550
<i>Let me introduce...</i>

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:49.300
<i>Burning Rescue's young hero,</i>

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:50.700
Galo Thymos!

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:56.370
<i>He annihilated Mad Burnish.
Let's praise his achievement.</i>

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:03.670
Galo, keep protecting Promepolis hereafter.

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:05.250
You bet I will, Governor.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:09.210
I'll protect this town,
 just like you saved me.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:13.640
You've always been my hero,

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:16.100
since the day you lost your arm to save me.

00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:33.250
I'm counting on you, Galo.

00:24:37.250 --> 00:24:41.000
Inferno Volcano Margherita Megamax.

00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:43.370
There you go.

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:52.470
Ouch. It's so yummy hot from the oven.

00:24:52.630 --> 00:24:53.260
Another one.

00:24:53.510 --> 00:24:54.340
Sure.

00:24:54.590 --> 00:24:57.470
Cooked just right, as usual.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.470
He's very good.

00:25:03.060 --> 00:25:05.190
There you go.

00:25:06.860 --> 00:25:09.820
I saw you on TV, Galo.
Great job.

00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:11.150
This?

00:25:11.650 --> 00:25:15.860
They were a real nuisance,
those terrorists.

00:25:15.860 --> 00:25:18.780
Mad Burnish,
is that what they're called?

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:21.620
It's a relief to know
their boss's in jail.

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:25.120
I'm sure not all Burnish
are dangerous like those guys.

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:28.000
But, they get discriminated
against because of them.

00:25:28.170 --> 00:25:30.550
You nailed it, chief.

00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:35.470
The Burnish are misunderstood.
They're not to blame.

00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:37.260
It's a mutation.

00:25:37.510 --> 00:25:41.180
They can do nothing about it.
The question is how you use it.

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:43.640
Like Vary's superhuman strength.

00:25:44.300 --> 00:25:48.150
Anyway, just count on me
for any fire in town.

00:25:48.150 --> 00:25:49.860
I sear on this medal.

00:25:50.020 --> 00:25:51.190
You're so reliable.

00:25:51.320 --> 00:25:52.570
We're counting on you.

00:25:55.650 --> 00:25:57.860
But, wearing it here?

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:00.910
A man must always wear
his medals on his chest.

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:04.910
All the more if Gov Kray
gave it to me.

00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:08.210
He saved your life, right?

00:26:08.670 --> 00:26:10.880
Yeah, when I was a kid.

00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:14.050
The governor was still a student back then.

00:26:14.050 --> 00:26:16.220
He got known thanks to that rescue.

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:19.550
Then his research on fireproof material got noticed,

00:26:19.550 --> 00:26:22.430
and he became a billionaire.

00:26:22.430 --> 00:26:25.020
Now he's the president of the Firesight Foundation

00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:26.980
and city governor.

00:26:27.600 --> 00:26:30.020
An amazing upstart route.

00:26:32.070 --> 00:26:34.440
Can't you make money
 with your inventions?

00:26:34.780 --> 00:26:37.400
Inventions that make money are a heresy.

00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:40.410
The true mad scientist.

00:26:40.780 --> 00:26:44.370
Your older sister's one too.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:50.790
Yeah. No idea what she's researching, though.

00:26:51.210 --> 00:26:54.170
Warp engines? They still have a long way to go.

00:26:54.590 --> 00:26:57.130
Will we be able to see 'em in our lifetime?

00:26:57.800 --> 00:27:01.680
I was able to become a rescuer
thanks to Gov Kray's help.

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:04.010
I gotta pay him back,
no matter what the risks.

00:27:04.470 --> 00:27:08.270
Chief!
More Inferno Volcano Margherita!

00:27:10.190 --> 00:27:12.310
We better not split the bill.

00:27:12.610 --> 00:27:13.310
Gimme that.

00:27:13.310 --> 00:27:14.900
You're eating too much.

00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:30.580
Freeze Force?

00:27:31.830 --> 00:27:34.750
Nobody move!

00:27:35.750 --> 00:27:38.760
If you do,
I'll regard you as a Burnish.

00:27:38.760 --> 00:27:41.180
Bastard!
What are you here for?

00:27:43.390 --> 00:27:47.060
You again?
Shut up and watch.

00:27:47.310 --> 00:27:49.930
Hey, you! Don't move.

00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:50.980
Hey!

00:27:52.150 --> 00:27:53.520
Stay away!

00:28:00.400 --> 00:28:02.160
You're a Burnish?

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:12.670
Please, wait!
What has he done wrong?

00:28:12.670 --> 00:28:15.210
He was only baking pizza.

00:28:15.290 --> 00:28:17.090
Did you know?

00:28:18.300 --> 00:28:19.590
Boss.

00:28:20.130 --> 00:28:21.220
It's okay.

00:28:21.300 --> 00:28:25.510
But, you just wanted
to make good pizza, didn't you?

00:28:25.600 --> 00:28:26.760
Owner.

00:28:27.390 --> 00:28:30.220
You're under arrest too.
Cordon off the store.

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:32.560
Wait.

00:28:32.980 --> 00:28:34.230
The burnish is innocent.

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:36.150
And Chief had
nothing to do with it.

00:28:36.400 --> 00:28:40.650
He violated the
Burnish Protection Crime Act.

00:28:40.650 --> 00:28:43.240
Whoever hides a Burnish
gets arrested too.

00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:48.330
You should start studying law
before posing as a hero.

00:28:48.870 --> 00:28:50.120
Wait!

00:28:50.500 --> 00:28:52.580
It's true, that law does exist.

00:28:52.580 --> 00:28:55.460
But, it's a special
anti-terrorism law.

00:28:55.460 --> 00:28:57.960
These people are not terrorists.

00:28:58.170 --> 00:29:01.800
That's for the court to decide.

00:29:09.350 --> 00:29:12.020
So, this pizza
was made by a Burnish?

00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:13.480
Disgusting.

00:29:13.520 --> 00:29:16.560
How can you give this stuff
to your customers?

00:29:16.900 --> 00:29:18.560
Hey! Stop it!

00:29:18.730 --> 00:29:19.610
Galo!

00:29:20.070 --> 00:29:24.150
Don't make a mistake.
We have no right to stop them.

00:29:24.150 --> 00:29:25.740
Pisses me off though.

00:29:32.160 --> 00:29:34.080
Where are you going?

00:29:37.670 --> 00:29:38.540
Get out.

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:42.340
We're transferring you.

00:29:47.430 --> 00:29:48.140
Gueira.

00:29:48.140 --> 00:29:48.470
Aye.

00:29:48.930 --> 00:29:49.680
Meis.

00:29:49.680 --> 00:29:49.970
Yes.

00:29:50.560 --> 00:29:51.680
Let's do it.

00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:08.950
Bastard!

00:30:09.990 --> 00:30:11.780
We Burnish are free.

00:30:12.040 --> 00:30:14.160
I won't let the Foundation do what they want.

00:30:16.580 --> 00:30:18.040
We'll take back our hurt brothers.

00:30:20.880 --> 00:30:21.920
Thanks.

00:30:22.250 --> 00:30:23.380
Free the others.

00:30:23.380 --> 00:30:23.670
Yup!

00:30:24.210 --> 00:30:25.550
But don't kill anyone.

00:30:25.550 --> 00:30:27.050
We Burnish don't kill without reason.

00:30:28.050 --> 00:30:29.260
I know!

00:30:35.060 --> 00:30:36.350
A wall of flames!

00:30:46.360 --> 00:30:48.150
Come on. We're breaking out.

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:49.610
You're...

00:30:49.860 --> 00:30:53.370
Breaking a freezing
 ring is a piece of cake for our boss.

00:30:53.870 --> 00:30:54.790
Come on!

00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:06.130
You're a nuisance.

00:31:16.640 --> 00:31:18.850
Come on, this way!
Quick!

00:31:34.030 --> 00:31:38.120
I didn't know about this place.
What is it?

00:31:38.370 --> 00:31:39.370
Dunno.

00:31:39.830 --> 00:31:41.500
You don't know?

00:31:41.580 --> 00:31:45.880
I found it by chance riding
around one day I was pissed off.

00:31:46.420 --> 00:31:49.550
Since then, I come here
to cool off.

00:31:49.630 --> 00:31:52.340
You really have to
go out of your way

00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:54.350
to come up here in the woods.

00:31:54.470 --> 00:31:57.350
Only someone with lots
of spare energy would do it.

00:31:57.680 --> 00:31:59.730
Why are you here, then?

00:31:59.890 --> 00:32:02.230
The way you took off,

00:32:02.230 --> 00:32:05.520
I thought you went to
raid Freeze Force HQ.

00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:07.020
You wanted to help?

00:32:07.230 --> 00:32:08.940
I wanted to stop you.

00:32:10.240 --> 00:32:12.820
You think I'm an idiot,
don't you?

00:32:13.070 --> 00:32:13.870
Yeah.

00:32:15.200 --> 00:32:15.910
Jeez.

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.410
Hey! It could break!

00:32:18.540 --> 00:32:23.040
No worries. I dug down 5 meters,
and there was ice all the way.

00:32:23.500 --> 00:32:25.380
You dug down 5 meters?

00:32:25.710 --> 00:32:28.920
Yeah. I was curious to see
how far down the ice went.

00:32:31.880 --> 00:32:34.470
Come on.
You can skate with shoes too.

00:32:37.600 --> 00:32:39.640
Well, I'm relieved.

00:32:40.390 --> 00:32:44.400
You've got enough sense
to come here and cool off.

00:32:44.770 --> 00:32:47.940
I can't give Gov Kray trouble.

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:53.750
The higher-ups know
he saved my life.

00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:55.780
If I did something wrong,

00:32:55.780 --> 00:32:59.910
they'd think I'm
misusing his authority.

00:33:00.660 --> 00:33:03.660
So you can be sensible.

00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:08.590
I guess I understand
how you feel.

00:33:09.340 --> 00:33:11.090
I'm the same.

00:33:11.460 --> 00:33:15.930
I've always been
"Heris's sister," not "Aina."

00:33:16.340 --> 00:33:20.970
She's always been very smart.
She was a child prodigy.

00:33:21.310 --> 00:33:21.970
I see.

00:33:22.890 --> 00:33:23.980
But...

00:33:24.690 --> 00:33:28.060
I'm proud of being
Heris Ardebit's sister.

00:33:28.560 --> 00:33:31.030
She's the core pillar
of Foresight Lab now.

00:33:31.320 --> 00:33:32.940
You're working hard too.

00:33:34.360 --> 00:33:35.820
You're you, Aina.

00:33:52.550 --> 00:33:53.670
Hey!

00:33:58.930 --> 00:33:59.890
...Burnish.

00:34:03.930 --> 00:34:04.730
Where are you going?

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:06.940
You call HQ.

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:12.020
Jeez! He's always like that.

00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:20.050
You're Mad Burnish's boss!

00:35:20.300 --> 00:35:21.640
Lio Fotia.

00:35:22.510 --> 00:35:24.890
I've already told you.
Memorize it, Galo Thymos.

00:35:25.390 --> 00:35:26.390
What?

00:35:27.890 --> 00:35:30.060
Be quiet.
We're having a meal.

00:35:30.350 --> 00:35:32.190
Do the Burnish eat food too?

00:35:39.530 --> 00:35:40.360
Ouch!

00:35:42.070 --> 00:35:44.100
What do you think we are?

00:35:44.500 --> 00:35:48.500
We Burnish are human beings.
If we don't eat, we die.

00:35:51.420 --> 00:35:52.670
Sorry.

00:35:53.170 --> 00:35:54.130
You're right.

00:35:55.250 --> 00:35:56.590
Lio.

00:36:00.590 --> 00:36:03.550
Hang on in there, Thyma.
The truck'll be here soon.

00:36:03.550 --> 00:36:04.500
<i>A truck?</i>

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:06.470
A helicopter'd be too conspicuous.

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:09.390
Gueira and Meis went to get a truck.

00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:12.650
But, she won't...

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:14.360
Let me do it!

00:36:16.610 --> 00:36:17.530
You?

00:36:18.320 --> 00:36:21.070
She's hurt because of you guys!

00:36:21.320 --> 00:36:23.280
I'm a rescuer.

00:36:23.280 --> 00:36:25.370
I did emergency medical care training.

00:36:25.570 --> 00:36:27.870
I carry medical equipment on my bike.

00:36:29.700 --> 00:36:30.700
No need.

00:37:30.470 --> 00:37:34.100
From flames to ashes, from ashes to earth.

00:37:34.850 --> 00:37:36.600
Rest in peace.

00:37:40.780 --> 00:37:42.280
She turned into ashes?

00:37:42.940 --> 00:37:44.650
It's the Burnish's fate.

00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:45.450
What?

00:37:45.820 --> 00:37:48.160
The flames burn our body.

00:37:48.160 --> 00:37:51.540
But they also give us
the power to regenerate it.

00:37:52.290 --> 00:37:55.210
While we're alive,
our body is eternal.

00:37:55.210 --> 00:37:57.370
We'll recover no matter
how much we burn.

00:37:57.670 --> 00:38:02.590
But, once our life is over,
we turn into ashes.

00:38:03.460 --> 00:38:04.510
Are you serious?

00:38:05.010 --> 00:38:08.650
That's no surprise at all.
All humans die.

00:38:08.650 --> 00:38:11.140
We feed the flames
and burn out.

00:38:11.560 --> 00:38:13.970
This certainty
is like a blessing.

00:38:14.060 --> 00:38:15.730
So, you live for the flames?

00:38:15.980 --> 00:38:19.690
We can hear them.
We hear their cries.

00:38:19.940 --> 00:38:22.730
"I want to burn harder!"

00:38:22.730 --> 00:38:24.780
"I want to blaze!
Stronger, hotter!"

00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:27.990
They are alive.

00:38:28.410 --> 00:38:31.530
Granting their wishes
is the Burnish's destiny.

00:38:33.200 --> 00:38:35.200
But, we don't kill people.

00:38:35.910 --> 00:38:37.960
When we Mad Burnish
attack a town,

00:38:37.960 --> 00:38:39.630
we always provide
an escape route.

00:38:40.420 --> 00:38:42.590
We pride ourselves for that.

00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:46.920
Boss, the truck is ready.

00:38:46.920 --> 00:38:47.800
There's room for everyone.

00:38:48.130 --> 00:38:48.930
Alright, let's go.

00:38:49.430 --> 00:38:50.890
It's dangerous to
stay here too long.

00:38:53.810 --> 00:38:55.270
Running away again?

00:38:56.810 --> 00:38:59.730
Yeah. As long as the
Foundation's after us.

00:38:59.770 --> 00:39:01.980
Can't you stop starting fires?

00:39:01.980 --> 00:39:05.230
You could live
like normal people if you did.

00:39:05.480 --> 00:39:07.190
You wouldn't have to run.

00:39:09.070 --> 00:39:10.820
Do you really believe that?

00:39:12.700 --> 00:39:13.280
Yeah.

00:39:14.790 --> 00:39:16.160
You're an idiot.

00:39:16.290 --> 00:39:17.370
What?

00:39:17.540 --> 00:39:19.670
Why do you think she died?

00:39:19.790 --> 00:39:22.290
Because of the 
Foresight Foundation's experiments.

00:39:24.250 --> 00:39:26.210
You really didn't know?

00:39:27.380 --> 00:39:28.880
What a simpleton.

00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:33.800
Not just her. Everyone was
 almost killed by Kray Foresight.

00:39:34.180 --> 00:39:39.230
He cuts us up and dissects us
 for his research.

00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:41.060
But, we're humans too.

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:42.440
You're lying!

00:39:43.060 --> 00:39:45.320
The governor'd never do something like that.

00:39:47.650 --> 00:39:50.570
Keep living in denial.

00:39:51.030 --> 00:39:54.240
Hey!
Wait! Hey!

00:39:54.530 --> 00:39:55.700
Wait!

00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:20.980
Galo! Are you OK?

00:40:37.530 --> 00:40:38.490
Galo.

00:40:40.830 --> 00:40:41.830
You want to return it?

00:40:42.160 --> 00:40:43.040
Yeah.

00:40:43.830 --> 00:40:46.040
Lio has escaped.

00:40:46.540 --> 00:40:49.250
Nobody reported that to me.

00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:53.380
I met him in a mountain cave.
He said he escaped from prison.

00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:57.010
Even if that was the truth,

00:40:57.010 --> 00:40:59.810
I can't see the need to return it.

00:41:00.060 --> 00:41:02.600
Medals are made to be awarded

00:41:02.600 --> 00:41:05.400
to and from people who deserve them.

00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:08.520
Neither of us is worthy.

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:11.110
What do you mean?

00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:16.070
Gov, is it true that
 you're doing human experiments

00:41:16.070 --> 00:41:17.250
with the Burnish?

00:41:25.290 --> 00:41:27.330
You're my hero.

00:41:27.330 --> 00:41:29.630
You saved me, started a foundation,

00:41:29.630 --> 00:41:31.710
and founded this amazing town.

00:41:32.420 --> 00:41:34.800
But, you're doing such a horrible thing?

00:41:35.180 --> 00:41:36.050
Horrible?

00:41:38.550 --> 00:41:39.850
The Burnish are humans.

00:41:40.100 --> 00:41:42.600
They get hungry, they get sad if they lose a friend.

00:41:42.680 --> 00:41:44.810
It's bad that they cause fires,

00:41:44.810 --> 00:41:46.810
but you can arrest them and that's it.

00:41:47.020 --> 00:41:49.190
You can't just kill them for no reason!

00:41:54.030 --> 00:41:54.990
I see.

00:41:57.280 --> 00:41:58.820
Follow me.

00:42:07.710 --> 00:42:10.750
Ever since the Burnish appeared 30 years ago,

00:42:10.750 --> 00:42:13.210
underground magma's been running out of control.

00:42:14.170 --> 00:42:15.340
At this rate,

00:42:15.340 --> 00:42:18.550
it'll gush out and cover
 the whole planet in six months.

00:42:18.680 --> 00:42:19.600
What?

00:42:27.350 --> 00:42:28.190
Oh?

00:42:33.530 --> 00:42:36.740
It'll be a greater catastrophe
than the Great World Blaze.

00:42:37.910 --> 00:42:40.320
The earth will become a dead planet.

00:42:40.950 --> 00:42:41.910
No way...

00:43:00.180 --> 00:43:02.930
So many doors.

00:43:05.640 --> 00:43:09.730
This is the Parnassus Project.
The last hope for mankind.

00:43:10.270 --> 00:43:12.900
A spaceship?

00:43:13.570 --> 00:43:15.320
There's a planet very similar to earth

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:17.490
four light-years from here.

00:43:17.650 --> 00:43:19.660
Omega Centauri.

00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:25.080
Starship Parnassus will be the new Noah's Ark.

00:43:25.080 --> 00:43:28.040
It'll carry 10,000 chosen ones

00:43:28.040 --> 00:43:29.500
who'll migrate to Omega Centauri.

00:43:30.710 --> 00:43:33.170
Only 10,000 people?

00:43:33.380 --> 00:43:37.210
That's the maximum number 
of passengers it can carry.

00:43:38.380 --> 00:43:40.090
You can't be serious...

00:43:50.980 --> 00:43:52.100
You're...

00:43:55.070 --> 00:43:56.730
Aina's sis?

00:43:59.240 --> 00:44:00.400
Why is he here?

00:44:00.780 --> 00:44:03.320
It's OK.
How's the project coming along?

00:44:03.450 --> 00:44:06.580
We're about to start the final test now.

00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:08.580
That's the pizza maker.

00:44:10.040 --> 00:44:10.960
What are you doing to him?

00:44:11.370 --> 00:44:12.830
Just watch.

00:44:12.960 --> 00:44:14.040
<i>Start the test.</i>

00:44:14.210 --> 00:44:15.290
Start the test.

00:44:15.420 --> 00:44:16.960
<i>Activate Prometech pod.</i>

00:44:28.270 --> 00:44:29.520
<i>Activate warp.</i>

00:44:31.350 --> 00:44:32.520
Activate warp.

00:44:39.360 --> 00:44:40.750
Stop Prometech pod.

00:44:40.900 --> 00:44:42.150
<i>Stop pod.</i>

00:44:42.240 --> 00:44:43.450
The test was successful.

00:44:44.360 --> 00:44:47.080
The implementation 
of the warp engine is in sight.

00:44:47.740 --> 00:44:49.200
I told you.

00:44:49.750 --> 00:44:51.660
We should have used the Prometech engine

00:44:51.660 --> 00:44:53.330
since the beginning.

00:44:55.130 --> 00:44:56.210
That's horrible.

00:44:56.670 --> 00:44:59.420
It's a valued sacrifice for the survival of mankind.

00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:00.920
What?

00:45:01.260 --> 00:45:04.430
We can't build the warp engine
 without the Burnish.

00:45:04.590 --> 00:45:06.470
There must be some other way.

00:45:06.470 --> 00:45:10.020
If we stop the magma, 
we won't need to go to another planet.

00:45:10.520 --> 00:45:13.440
I've considered that.

00:45:13.440 --> 00:45:17.400
But, we can't stop it with our current technology.

00:45:17.400 --> 00:45:19.230
Migration's our best bet.

00:45:19.730 --> 00:45:22.610
So, you sacrifice the Burnish for that?

00:45:22.740 --> 00:45:23.900
Exactly.

00:45:24.400 --> 00:45:26.660
Do you understand what I'm doing now?

00:45:27.160 --> 00:45:28.740
Yeah, I do.

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:30.620
But I can't accept it.

00:45:31.580 --> 00:45:33.120
Then, what will you do?

00:45:33.620 --> 00:45:36.880
I'll extinguish the Earth's magma!

00:45:39.460 --> 00:45:41.550
I knew you'd say that.

00:45:43.720 --> 00:45:44.800
We're short of time.

00:45:44.800 --> 00:45:47.300
Can't have an idiot making a fuss.

00:45:48.300 --> 00:45:48.890
Why, Gov?

00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:52.890
Don't call me "Gov!"

00:45:58.350 --> 00:46:01.980
I've always hated it.

00:46:03.440 --> 00:46:06.320
You've always been an eyesore to me!

00:46:07.490 --> 00:46:08.820
Take him away.

00:46:09.830 --> 00:46:13.450
What the hell?
What's going on, Kray?

00:46:15.050 --> 00:46:15.830
Kray...

00:46:15.960 --> 00:46:17.650
Begin final tuning.

00:46:18.130 --> 00:46:20.670
We'll install the Prometech engine 
on the Parnassus.

00:46:21.550 --> 00:46:22.920
Biar, call the car.

00:46:23.090 --> 00:46:23.840
Yes, Sir.

00:46:27.590 --> 00:46:30.220
Hey! Open the door!

00:46:30.850 --> 00:46:33.850
Hey! Anybody there?

00:46:33.850 --> 00:46:36.940
Please, open the door!

00:46:39.350 --> 00:46:41.110
Why, Kray?

00:46:42.190 --> 00:46:45.320
You were my hero.

00:46:50.780 --> 00:46:52.750
I was against it.

00:46:53.650 --> 00:46:56.330
Pod production is already complete.

00:46:56.620 --> 00:46:58.670
You were planning to use the Prometech engine

00:46:58.670 --> 00:46:59.750
since the start?

00:46:59.920 --> 00:47:03.300
Yes. I was only waiting for you
 to make the decision.

00:47:04.420 --> 00:47:05.800
How could you...

00:47:06.380 --> 00:47:09.130
We'll have to abandon most of 
mankind to its fate.

00:47:09.130 --> 00:47:14.350
You couldn't live with it
 if it wasn't your own decision.

00:47:15.720 --> 00:47:17.640
How's the Burnish crackdown going?

00:47:17.810 --> 00:47:20.400
Freeze Force has already been deployed.

00:47:20.650 --> 00:47:23.520
Checkmate.
We'll get busy.

00:47:36.200 --> 00:47:39.790
We're almost there. Give it your all.

00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:42.830
Who knew they were hiding here.

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.750
"The darkest place is under the candlestick."

00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:48.260
Didn't notice with all these volcanos around.

00:47:58.060 --> 00:47:59.480
Wait!

00:48:06.650 --> 00:48:09.610
Run away!
Freeze Force's here!

00:48:48.530 --> 00:48:51.280
Careful. We don't want 'em dead.

00:48:51.610 --> 00:48:54.030
They're precious fuel.

00:49:06.960 --> 00:49:08.420
How did you find us?

00:49:09.630 --> 00:49:12.760
Who knows?
Take a wild guess.

00:49:15.640 --> 00:49:17.220
Be careful.

00:49:27.020 --> 00:49:28.190
Boss!

00:49:28.190 --> 00:49:29.940
You bastard!

00:49:30.480 --> 00:49:32.650
I was waiting for you,
Mr. Vulcan.

00:49:33.400 --> 00:49:35.360
You told him.

00:49:35.820 --> 00:49:36.820
Get 'em!

00:49:41.240 --> 00:49:45.120
We put a tracker in the old man's body beforehand.

00:49:45.330 --> 00:49:46.330
That was foolish.

00:49:46.750 --> 00:49:49.540
You're the fool.

00:49:49.540 --> 00:49:52.300
We're no match against 
the Foundation.

00:49:52.510 --> 00:49:53.920
The shorter the time you've got left,

00:49:53.920 --> 00:49:56.220
the more you think about yourself.

00:49:57.090 --> 00:49:58.680
Thanks for your hard work.

00:50:00.970 --> 00:50:02.180
Oh?

00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:05.140
Resources are limited; can't let him go to waste.

00:50:05.140 --> 00:50:07.810
Even an old man should make himself useful.

00:50:07.900 --> 00:50:09.060
You bastard!

00:50:10.690 --> 00:50:13.530
Absolte Zero Chain Freezing Bullet.

00:50:13.530 --> 00:50:16.490
It freezes by absorbing your body heat.

00:50:16.490 --> 00:50:19.120
Good luck burning through that.

00:50:20.490 --> 00:50:25.620
I knew you got caught on purpose to free the prisoners.

00:50:25.620 --> 00:50:28.170
Thought you outsmarted us, huh?

00:50:30.670 --> 00:50:33.130
We saw you coming a mile away, brat!

00:50:36.630 --> 00:50:37.800
No dice!

00:50:38.550 --> 00:50:41.550
You've even gathered all the Burnish

00:50:41.550 --> 00:50:43.810
in one spot, saving us time.

00:50:44.770 --> 00:50:47.350
Gotta thank you for that.

00:50:54.280 --> 00:50:56.030
How dare you hit the boss!

00:50:57.650 --> 00:50:58.860
How dare you hit the settlement!

00:51:04.580 --> 00:51:06.080
You'll pay for it!

00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:19.550
Stop it! Run away!

00:51:19.680 --> 00:51:20.720
Forget about us!

00:51:20.720 --> 00:51:22.600
Burnish's flame will continue 
to burn so long as you're alive!

00:51:22.850 --> 00:51:25.930
Your flames are invincible!

00:51:26.020 --> 00:51:27.100
No...

00:51:33.650 --> 00:51:35.400
You bastards!

00:51:37.490 --> 00:51:38.780
Go!

00:51:40.780 --> 00:51:41.780
Guys!

00:51:44.830 --> 00:51:46.120
We did it!

00:51:51.250 --> 00:51:53.080
You smart asses.

00:51:58.550 --> 00:52:00.430
Where was Lio shot out to?

00:52:00.470 --> 00:52:02.220
Inside Fennel Volcano.

00:52:02.340 --> 00:52:05.510
We don't have 
the right equipment to go in there.

00:52:05.810 --> 00:52:10.940
Doesn't matter. Absolute zero bullets'll 
surely take his life.

00:53:35.650 --> 00:53:36.690
Governor.

00:53:37.190 --> 00:53:38.360
The test was a success.

00:53:38.480 --> 00:53:42.360
Yes, so I see.
Well done, Dr. Heris.

00:53:43.150 --> 00:53:45.820
Commence the Parnassus Project now.

00:53:46.160 --> 00:53:46.870
Yes, sir.

00:53:47.320 --> 00:53:49.660
We'll start contacting selected citizens

00:53:49.660 --> 00:53:51.410
in accordance to simulations.

00:53:59.250 --> 00:54:00.550
Did you find him?

00:54:01.800 --> 00:54:04.670
No. He wasn't even at the frozen lake.

00:54:10.100 --> 00:54:14.560
We lost his tracks after he
 went to the governor's.

00:54:14.890 --> 00:54:16.770
It's been a week already.

00:54:17.100 --> 00:54:20.190
Jeez, where'd he go?

00:54:20.190 --> 00:54:22.980
There's so much new stuff I want to test.

00:54:23.230 --> 00:54:27.280
I'd like both of you to 
refrain from acting selfishly.

00:54:27.610 --> 00:54:29.950
My inventions are not selfish.

00:54:29.950 --> 00:54:32.290
They're a precaution, you never know.

00:54:32.450 --> 00:54:33.290
Yeah, yeah.

00:54:34.250 --> 00:54:35.250
That idiot.

00:54:38.210 --> 00:54:39.580
I finally found out.

00:54:39.580 --> 00:54:42.460
A friend at the city office told me Galo 
was arrested.

00:54:43.050 --> 00:54:44.630
What? How come?

00:54:44.710 --> 00:54:47.130
They say he's a terrorist.

00:54:47.130 --> 00:54:50.430
He got arrested trying to shoot the governor.

00:54:50.850 --> 00:54:51.930
No way!

00:54:52.810 --> 00:54:54.520
What do you think, Captain?

00:54:54.850 --> 00:54:56.980
It's a fact he was arrested.

00:54:58.050 --> 00:55:00.500
Sounds kinda fishy.

00:55:02.480 --> 00:55:03.110
Hey!

00:55:06.360 --> 00:55:08.070
Aina! Where are you going?

00:55:13.490 --> 00:55:17.620
Wait outside. Don't worry, 
I'll shout if I need help.

00:55:29.340 --> 00:55:30.430
Are you sure?

00:55:30.800 --> 00:55:34.060
You're not the kind of guy 
who'd attack an unarmed person.

00:55:35.060 --> 00:55:39.640
Aina often told me you're honest and straightforward to a fault.

00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:44.110
Come on, eat.
It's your last supper.

00:55:47.820 --> 00:55:49.320
You really OK with this?

00:55:50.110 --> 00:55:53.030
Aina told me she's proud of you.

00:55:53.030 --> 00:55:55.080
Does she know about the migration?

00:55:55.080 --> 00:55:56.450
And about the Burnish?

00:55:56.540 --> 00:55:58.580
It's none of your business.

00:55:59.080 --> 00:56:02.250
You haven't told her.
She wouldn't have taken it.

00:56:02.960 --> 00:56:05.420
Why don't you tell her,
if you have nothing to hide?

00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:11.260
I'd do anything for her.
For her survival.

00:56:12.800 --> 00:56:15.050
I don't think she'd be happy.

00:56:22.270 --> 00:56:23.400
Heris!

00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:24.810
Aina.

00:56:26.150 --> 00:56:27.980
Is it true that Galo was arrested?

00:56:28.480 --> 00:56:29.320
Yes.

00:56:29.530 --> 00:56:31.990
There must be a mistake.
He's no terrorist.

00:56:31.990 --> 00:56:34.780
Please, talk to Governor Kray.

00:56:35.200 --> 00:56:36.830
Calm down, Aina.

00:56:37.040 --> 00:56:37.740
But...

00:56:38.200 --> 00:56:40.040
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:56:40.040 --> 00:56:41.910
He tried to assault the governor.

00:56:45.340 --> 00:56:46.750
Listen, Aina.

00:56:46.750 --> 00:56:50.340
You must think about yourself now.

00:56:50.630 --> 00:56:52.010
I'll contact you soon.

00:56:52.010 --> 00:56:54.470
Come here as soon as you get the call.

00:56:55.510 --> 00:56:56.390
Understand?

00:56:59.930 --> 00:57:01.800
I love you, Aina.

00:57:02.700 --> 00:57:04.100
Heris...

00:57:50.690 --> 00:57:51.900
I won't forgive you.

00:57:53.190 --> 00:57:54.990
I'll make you pay,

00:57:54.990 --> 00:57:58.160
Kray Foresight!

00:58:10.090 --> 00:58:14.130
You'll bear the brunt of the Burnish's fury!

00:58:37.860 --> 00:58:38.570
What happened?

00:58:38.660 --> 00:58:41.280
<i>Unexplained fires in all areas of Promepolis.</i>

00:58:41.280 --> 00:58:43.910
<i>A huge Burnish Flare's 
coming out from the ground.</i>

00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:46.250
This is a warning for Kray Foresigh.

00:58:46.250 --> 00:58:49.830
Free all captured Burnish immediately.

00:58:49.830 --> 00:58:53.090
Otherwise I'll burn Promepolis to the ground.

00:58:53.090 --> 00:58:54.920
I'll have no mercy.

00:59:02.180 --> 00:59:04.140
Lio? Is that Lio?

00:59:09.230 --> 00:59:10.440
That flame...

00:59:11.770 --> 00:59:13.150
He's crying?

00:59:20.410 --> 00:59:25.950
Lio Fotia, I'm surprised you're still alive. 
You're a bad loser.

00:59:32.210 --> 00:59:35.650
You're an eyesore.
Get lost!

00:59:43.140 --> 00:59:44.640
Don't mess with me!

01:00:12.040 --> 01:00:13.330
Stupid eyelid!

01:00:20.590 --> 01:00:22.720
Enough with the cannon fodder.

01:00:23.590 --> 01:00:26.720
Come out and face me, Kray Foresight!

01:00:34.730 --> 01:00:36.730
The fire's moving fast.

01:00:37.190 --> 01:00:39.030
Captain, this is endless!

01:00:39.280 --> 01:00:41.650
Captain, all Freeze Force interceptors

01:00:41.650 --> 01:00:43.490
have been shot down.

01:00:45.070 --> 01:00:48.040
Varys, go to area C-5, the most damaged.

01:00:48.040 --> 01:00:50.120
We'll keep the fire under control.

01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:51.200
Yessir!

01:00:57.960 --> 01:00:58.670
Galo?

01:00:58.800 --> 01:00:59.920
Captain?

01:01:00.050 --> 01:01:03.380
Captain! The Fire!
A big fire's moving!

01:01:03.630 --> 01:01:05.090
On your ass.

01:01:05.720 --> 01:01:08.760
Oww! It's hot! Ow!

01:01:08.760 --> 01:01:10.730
Ow! Ow! Ow!

01:01:10.930 --> 01:01:13.190
I'm coming too, Captain.

01:01:14.730 --> 01:01:16.860
But, you're...

01:01:16.860 --> 01:01:18.400
We'll talk later.

01:01:18.650 --> 01:01:21.990
The fire's first priority.
Am I wrong?

01:01:22.490 --> 01:01:23.990
Did you escape?

01:01:24.110 --> 01:01:24.950
Yeah.

01:01:25.200 --> 01:01:26.160
Galo!

01:01:26.450 --> 01:01:27.950
I'm Gal Thymos!

01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.660
A firefighter with a burning soul!

01:01:29.830 --> 01:01:31.450
Where else would I go!

01:01:32.290 --> 01:01:32.960
Yeah.

01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:36.920
I serviced it.
Under Captain's orders.

01:01:37.380 --> 01:01:38.420
<i>Captain.</i>

01:01:38.750 --> 01:01:39.130
Yeah.

01:01:39.250 --> 01:01:40.920
Leave it to me!

01:01:41.420 --> 01:01:42.300
<i>Aina!</i>

01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:35.770
Mad Burnish.
I'm here.

01:02:37.060 --> 01:02:37.900
Kray.

01:02:40.610 --> 01:02:41.770
Kray!

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:47.490
Kray Foresight!

01:02:52.240 --> 01:02:53.290
Bring it on...

01:02:54.830 --> 01:02:56.790
Mad Burnish!

01:03:07.470 --> 01:03:10.510
Ow! It's hot!

01:03:12.560 --> 01:03:15.850
Stay out of it!

01:03:16.850 --> 01:03:21.690
It's not hot at all!

01:03:22.020 --> 01:03:27.650
Your spiteful flames aren't hot at all.

01:03:27.950 --> 01:03:32.450
My burning firefighter's soul's a million and ten times...

01:03:34.490 --> 01:03:37.200
hotter!

01:03:38.460 --> 01:03:40.370
It's cold!

01:04:10.240 --> 01:04:11.410
So be it.

01:04:20.830 --> 01:04:23.290
You again, Galo Thymos!

01:04:23.420 --> 01:04:25.210
I understand your anger.

01:04:25.210 --> 01:04:26.960
I was betrayed by Kray too.

01:04:27.090 --> 01:04:27.460
What?

01:04:27.590 --> 01:04:29.090
Having said that,

01:04:29.090 --> 01:04:33.140
I can't let you hurt 
and kill innocent civilians!

01:04:33.140 --> 01:04:35.140
You're the ones who're using

01:04:35.140 --> 01:04:37.470
innocent Burnish in human experiments!

01:04:37.560 --> 01:04:41.890
Didn't you guys pride 
yourselves for not killing without reason?

01:04:45.480 --> 01:04:49.400
<i>You two, try to cool off a little!</i>

01:04:53.660 --> 01:04:56.660
Ow! It's hot! It's hot!

01:05:21.890 --> 01:05:23.730
Did you calm down a bit?

01:05:23.810 --> 01:05:25.770
<i>Hey! What's that?</i>

01:05:31.900 --> 01:05:33.780
What is this place?

01:05:34.990 --> 01:05:37.120
The building's not wet.

01:05:37.620 --> 01:05:40.790
It was in a cavity under the ice.

01:05:40.910 --> 01:05:42.620
<i>Exactly.</i>

01:05:43.330 --> 01:05:46.080
<i>Welcome,
Galo Thymos and Lio Fotia.</i>

01:05:46.250 --> 01:05:48.040
How do you know our names?

01:05:48.250 --> 01:05:49.630
Who are you?

01:05:49.800 --> 01:05:53.220
<i>I need to talk to you.
Come with me.</i>

01:05:59.810 --> 01:06:00.720
<i>Wait a minute,</i>

01:06:01.180 --> 01:06:02.270
<i>you two!</i>

01:06:12.480 --> 01:06:13.990
We managed to contain the blaze.

01:06:14.110 --> 01:06:16.610
Incredible,
That dummy's attack worked.

01:06:16.740 --> 01:06:18.320
Fight or flight response.

01:06:18.570 --> 01:06:20.910
No man, it was simply a dummy's response.

01:06:21.240 --> 01:06:22.370
And Aina?

01:06:22.370 --> 01:06:24.370
Can't reach her since she went with the dummy.

01:06:25.460 --> 01:06:27.420
We have no time to worry about them.

01:06:27.830 --> 01:06:29.420
We've got rescue work to do.

01:06:29.500 --> 01:06:30.340
Roger!

01:06:31.840 --> 01:06:35.220
Governor, the fires in town
 were extinguished.

01:06:35.220 --> 01:06:37.720
The transport network 
is going back to normal.

01:06:37.840 --> 01:06:40.600
Good. Bring selected citizens on board

01:06:40.600 --> 01:06:42.890
and keep the others away from the ship.

01:06:43.220 --> 01:06:44.770
Parnassus is taking off.

01:06:46.640 --> 01:06:49.560
Activity in the earth's core has intensified.

01:06:49.560 --> 01:06:51.520
There's no time left.

01:07:19.760 --> 01:07:21.640
What is this place?

01:07:21.890 --> 01:07:24.140
Some kind of research facility?

01:07:25.600 --> 01:07:28.600
<i>So, you're not going 
to announce the Prometech pod?</i>

01:07:28.850 --> 01:07:34.360
<i>No. It's an evil invention 
that sacrifices Burnish lives.</i>

01:07:34.610 --> 01:07:38.280
<i>I see.
You've kept it secret, right?</i>

01:07:38.490 --> 01:07:40.610
<i>Only the two of us know.</i>

01:07:40.950 --> 01:07:42.320
<i>Same for the Promare?</i>

01:07:42.780 --> 01:07:43.620
<i>Correct.</i>

01:07:43.740 --> 01:07:45.580
<i>I'm relieved.</i>

01:07:47.160 --> 01:07:50.250
<i>Someone has to shoulder the fate of mankind.</i>

01:07:50.250 --> 01:07:52.210
<i>If you won't, then I will.</i>

01:07:52.210 --> 01:07:53.880
<i>No. I should be the one regardless.</i>

01:07:54.000 --> 01:07:56.260
<i>You... My research...</i>

01:07:56.380 --> 01:07:58.350
<i>Yes. I'm taking it all.</i>

01:07:58.350 --> 01:08:00.720
<i>Was this your plan all along?</i>

01:08:00.970 --> 01:08:02.930
<i>Maybe.</i>

01:08:11.270 --> 01:08:13.560
The governor's a murderer.

01:08:13.900 --> 01:08:16.530
The victim was the guy who took us here.

01:08:16.820 --> 01:08:18.820
<i>Exactly.
Kray killed me.</i>

01:08:20.030 --> 01:08:20.740
Who are you?

01:08:20.820 --> 01:08:24.330
<i>Deus Prometh.
I was a Burnish researcher.</i>

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:27.540
Instant freezing agent,
fireproof armor.

01:08:27.540 --> 01:08:30.850
They're all anti-Burnish patents
 belonging to the Foundation.

01:08:30.850 --> 01:08:33.540
<i>They're all my inventions.</i>

01:08:33.540 --> 01:08:36.210
<i>Kray stole them and registered them in his name.</i>

01:08:36.340 --> 01:08:38.170
So, what are you?

01:08:38.960 --> 01:08:42.720
<i>I backed up my consciousness
 into this computer.</i>

01:08:42.720 --> 01:08:45.100
<i>So that I could come back to life</i>

01:08:45.100 --> 01:08:47.350
<i>after my vital signs ceased.</i>

01:08:47.350 --> 01:08:50.100
<i>Of course, I made sure Kray didn't find out.</i>

01:08:50.100 --> 01:08:52.060
A virtual personality.

01:08:52.140 --> 01:08:54.520
How did you know our names?

01:08:54.770 --> 01:08:58.150
<i>I've been hacking Promepolis's network.</i>

01:08:58.150 --> 01:09:00.900
<i>I stay informed on whatever happens there</i>

01:09:00.900 --> 01:09:02.990
<i>in order to keep an eye on Kray.</i>

01:09:03.950 --> 01:09:04.660
What's that?

01:09:04.780 --> 01:09:05.570
That's...!

01:09:31.520 --> 01:09:34.650
<i>Volcanic eruption
in South-West Promepolis.</i>

01:09:35.350 --> 01:09:36.810
How's magma activity?

01:09:36.980 --> 01:09:39.250
<i>Within calculations.</i>

01:09:39.860 --> 01:09:42.570
Good. Get ready for departure.

01:09:42.690 --> 01:09:44.860
Boarding is complete.

01:09:45.360 --> 01:09:46.820
Please wait, Governor.

01:09:47.240 --> 01:09:47.830
What is it?

01:09:48.280 --> 01:09:49.910
Aina's not back yet.

01:09:50.080 --> 01:09:53.460
We've issued the order.
But we couldn't reach her.

01:09:53.580 --> 01:09:56.080
Don't take off until she's back.

01:09:56.210 --> 01:09:57.420
What are you saying?

01:09:57.540 --> 01:10:00.090
It'll all be meaningless if she doesn't survive!

01:10:00.170 --> 01:10:01.920
I'll wait until the last minute.

01:10:01.920 --> 01:10:05.380
But, we can't postpone because of her.

01:10:05.380 --> 01:10:07.050
You should know that.

01:10:09.260 --> 01:10:11.810
Go back to your post,
Dr. Heris.

01:10:13.480 --> 01:10:14.350
Kray...

01:10:16.520 --> 01:10:17.350
Now.

01:10:20.770 --> 01:10:21.940
What's that?

01:10:22.070 --> 01:10:23.740
It's a spaceship.

01:10:23.740 --> 01:10:25.450
Kray showed it to me at the lab.

01:10:25.450 --> 01:10:25.820
What?

01:10:26.280 --> 01:10:28.350
Soon the magma'll gush out and the Earth'll go

01:10:31.580 --> 01:10:34.290
So, they'll run away to another planet.

01:10:34.290 --> 01:10:36.710
Max 10,000 people can board it.

01:10:37.040 --> 01:10:38.580
<i>Only 10,000?</i>

01:10:38.880 --> 01:10:41.340
Yeah. On top of that, it's human-powered.

01:10:43.050 --> 01:10:46.930
They'll use the Burnish's flames
 to power the warp engine.

01:10:46.930 --> 01:10:50.180
And that'll chip away at their life.

01:10:50.300 --> 01:10:51.220
What?

01:10:51.390 --> 01:10:52.390
It's horrible.

01:10:53.350 --> 01:10:57.060
Galo, is that what my sister's 
been working on?

01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:00.190
It is, right?

01:11:00.480 --> 01:11:01.400
Yeah.

01:11:01.860 --> 01:11:05.400
<i>Kray, that fool.
Doesn't he realize?</i>

01:11:05.400 --> 01:11:08.200
<i>The moment he ignites that</i>

01:11:08.200 --> 01:11:10.280
<i>incomplete engine, the Earth'll perish.</i>

01:11:10.410 --> 01:11:11.410
What?

01:11:11.490 --> 01:11:14.290
<i>If he hurts the Burnish
 with the Prometech engine,</i>

01:11:14.290 --> 01:11:17.540
<i>the Promare in the Earth's core
 will go out of control.</i>

01:11:17.540 --> 01:11:19.210
<i>The plannet will be doomed.</i>

01:11:19.290 --> 01:11:20.330
What do you mean?

01:11:20.630 --> 01:11:24.510
<i>The flames the Burnish 
use are not regular flames.</i>

01:11:24.510 --> 01:11:28.340
<i>They're a fire life form from a parallel universe.</i>

01:11:28.510 --> 01:11:30.390
"Fire life form?"

01:11:30.890 --> 01:11:33.200
<i>I called them "Promare."</i>

01:11:33.890 --> 01:11:34.390
Promare?

01:11:34.890 --> 01:11:38.520
<i>Yes. Together they form a sentient</i>

01:11:38.520 --> 01:11:40.690
<i>fixed star in the parallel universe.</i>

01:11:40.690 --> 01:11:41.810
<i>In other words,</i>

01:11:41.810 --> 01:11:44.610
<i>it's an aggregate of living organisms</i>

01:11:44.610 --> 01:11:47.490
<i>achieving life through nuclear fusion</i>

01:11:47.490 --> 01:11:50.490
<i>and consciousness via electromagnetic field.</i>

01:11:50.490 --> 01:11:53.910
<i>What's seen as flames is but a fraction of energy</i>

01:11:53.910 --> 01:11:56.200
<i>seeping through a space-time rupture.</i>

01:11:57.080 --> 01:11:58.870
What's this old man saying?

01:11:59.250 --> 01:12:02.380
<i>30 years ago, there was 
a distortion of space and time</i>

01:12:02.380 --> 01:12:05.920
<i>that connected Earth's core to the Promare Universe.</i>

01:12:06.510 --> 01:12:11.050
<i>Humans prone to resonate with the Promare can use their power.</i>

01:12:12.090 --> 01:12:13.720
The Burnish?

01:12:13.890 --> 01:12:15.350
<i>That's right.</i>

01:12:15.680 --> 01:12:18.430
The voices that push us to burn stronger...

01:12:18.430 --> 01:12:20.140
It's the fire life forms.

01:12:21.060 --> 01:12:23.610
If that's the case, what have we been...

01:12:24.230 --> 01:12:27.780
<i>Using the Promare's interdimensional energy,</i>

01:12:27.780 --> 01:12:30.300
<i>teleportation is indeed possible.</i>

01:12:30.300 --> 01:12:32.950
<i>But, the Burnish's nerve signals reach the</i>

01:12:32.950 --> 01:12:35.950
<i>Promare they're synched with.</i>

01:12:36.200 --> 01:12:38.500
<i>The Promare feel the Burnish's pain.</i>

01:12:39.200 --> 01:12:41.540
<i>If those incomplete Prometech pods</i>

01:12:41.540 --> 01:12:44.840
<i>cause the Burnish enough pain,</i>

01:12:44.840 --> 01:12:47.630
<i>the Promare in Earth's core will spiral out of control,</i>

01:12:47.630 --> 01:12:49.720
<i>destroying the planet.</i>

01:12:50.670 --> 01:12:53.090
So, they're at the center of the Earth?

01:12:53.340 --> 01:12:56.510
<i>That's where the space-time rupture is.</i>

01:12:56.510 --> 01:12:58.020
<i>It is there they live.</i>

01:12:58.520 --> 01:12:59.470
<i>Galo Thymos.</i>

01:12:59.600 --> 01:13:01.140
<i>Lio Fotia.</i>

01:13:01.810 --> 01:13:04.150
<i>I want you to stop Kray Foresight.</i>

01:13:06.900 --> 01:13:07.820
Us?

01:13:07.980 --> 01:13:13.070
<i>Yes. With the real Prometech engine I've completed.</i>

01:13:13.200 --> 01:13:14.240
How?

01:13:14.410 --> 01:13:15.620
With this.

01:13:18.540 --> 01:13:21.500
<i>The super weapon I've created</i>

01:13:21.500 --> 01:13:23.210
<i>in the event of Promare disaster.</i>

01:13:23.750 --> 01:13:26.250
<i>Deus X Machina!</i>

01:13:31.260 --> 01:13:32.920
Interesting.

01:13:33.340 --> 01:13:35.390
They're already on board.

01:13:35.840 --> 01:13:39.640
<i>The completed Prometech engine
 doesn't cause pain.</i>

01:13:39.640 --> 01:13:44.770
<i>It uses Lio's body as a gateway
 to harness Promare energy.</i>

01:13:44.770 --> 01:13:48.520
<i>You just concentrate on synchronization.</i>

01:13:54.280 --> 01:13:55.820
Why us?

01:13:56.370 --> 01:13:58.740
Why did you choose me and this guy?

01:13:59.030 --> 01:14:02.040
<i>I didn't choose you.
You just happened to land here.</i>

01:14:02.790 --> 01:14:05.170
<i>I had to stop Kray,</i>

01:14:05.170 --> 01:14:07.500
<i>but I couldn't do anything by myself.</i>

01:14:07.500 --> 01:14:10.000
<i>Then you showed up.</i>

01:14:10.000 --> 01:14:12.010
<i>Mankind's still got luck on its side.</i>

01:14:12.170 --> 01:14:14.680
What if they didn't come?

01:14:14.840 --> 01:14:17.590
<i>Meh. Kray would've 
just doomed the Earth, I guess.</i>

01:14:17.680 --> 01:14:19.100
This guy...

01:14:19.220 --> 01:14:24.060
<i>I am no "guy," I'm a computer.
Now, the rest is in your hands.</i>

01:14:24.060 --> 01:14:25.980
<i>My job here is done.</i>

01:14:26.140 --> 01:14:28.060
<i>Professor? Professor!</i>

01:14:36.610 --> 01:14:38.070
Feeling conflicted?

01:14:39.350 --> 01:14:41.280
I guess you are.

01:14:41.280 --> 01:14:44.040
Your flames are aliens,
 that's a hell of a surprise.

01:14:44.200 --> 01:14:46.250
What do you know?

01:14:46.460 --> 01:14:48.330
Nothing, but if there's a fire,

01:14:48.330 --> 01:14:51.420
I'll put it out.
That's the only thing I know.

01:14:51.420 --> 01:14:53.260
So, you burn out too.

01:14:53.710 --> 01:14:54.050
What?

01:14:54.800 --> 01:14:58.220
Show off your Burnish pride.
That's what I mean.

01:15:00.300 --> 01:15:01.010
Yeah.

01:15:01.760 --> 01:15:05.770
Let's do this. We'll save the Burnish and the Earth.

01:15:05.890 --> 01:15:07.600
That's it.

01:15:13.900 --> 01:15:16.190
Ready for departure.

01:15:16.450 --> 01:15:18.950
Start the Prometech engine.

01:15:20.570 --> 01:15:23.870
Prometech engine.
Start.

01:15:43.350 --> 01:15:44.100
<i>That's...</i>

01:15:44.180 --> 01:15:47.350
The warp gate.
Keep going, Dr. Heris.

01:15:47.850 --> 01:15:50.690
Behold, the door to mankind's future opens.

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:51.980
What's that?

01:15:53.480 --> 01:15:53.980
What?

01:15:54.190 --> 01:15:56.100
Weird. Eruptions are happening

01:15:56.100 --> 01:15:58.200
<i>simultaneously all over the world.</i>

01:16:10.290 --> 01:16:11.600
The time has come.

01:16:12.750 --> 01:16:15.420
<i>Large unidentified machine ahead.</i>

01:16:15.420 --> 01:16:16.510
<i>Inbound and unresponsive.</i>

01:16:17.300 --> 01:16:18.170
That machine!

01:16:18.510 --> 01:16:20.090
Attack with all weapons!

01:16:21.090 --> 01:16:22.340
Shoot freezing missiles.

01:16:22.390 --> 01:16:24.810
Use regular munitions too.

01:16:25.310 --> 01:16:27.520
That's an order.

01:16:39.300 --> 01:16:41.950
<i>Collision on deck.
Target halted.</i>

01:16:42.950 --> 01:16:44.030
Is it dead?

01:16:45.580 --> 01:16:49.290
What are you doing?
You're the pilot!

01:16:49.660 --> 01:16:52.960
My bad.
Just can't get into the zone.

01:16:53.080 --> 01:16:54.130
What do you mean?

01:16:54.290 --> 01:16:55.960
Must be the way it looks.

01:16:56.500 --> 01:16:58.920
I mean, look how lame this design is.

01:16:58.920 --> 01:17:00.800
My firefighter's soul can't burn in that.

01:17:01.170 --> 01:17:03.590
You insist I come and this is the crap I get?

01:17:04.050 --> 01:17:07.310
So what do you want me to do?
Fine. How's this?

01:17:08.270 --> 01:17:09.750
Now we're talking!

01:17:09.980 --> 01:17:11.480
That's the stuff!

01:17:12.770 --> 01:17:15.110
This is my jam!

01:17:15.230 --> 01:17:18.110
Extremely strong Burnish signal.

01:17:18.110 --> 01:17:21.030
More pure than our Prometech engine.

01:17:27.530 --> 01:17:30.580
Even if the ideals you look up to

01:17:30.580 --> 01:17:34.000
fall to the ground, hope never breaks.

01:17:34.500 --> 01:17:37.670
A burning firefighter and a cool flame,

01:17:37.880 --> 01:17:40.550
oil and water as one!

01:17:41.970 --> 01:17:46.090
Absolute Firefighter Lio De Galon!

01:17:47.500 --> 01:17:53.310
We'll put out every last fire on Earth!

01:17:57.400 --> 01:17:59.250
What's that nonsense?

01:17:59.450 --> 01:18:02.240
"Deus X Machina"
doesn't have enough impact.

01:18:02.610 --> 01:18:05.160
Its name's Lio De Galon.

01:18:05.160 --> 01:18:08.410
You should praise my modesty
 for not calling it Galo De Lion.

01:18:08.620 --> 01:18:09.780
Shut up and pilot.

01:18:10.950 --> 01:18:15.080
As I thought, that's Deus X Machina.

01:18:15.080 --> 01:18:16.920
I didn't know it was completed.

01:18:27.180 --> 01:18:29.260
Was that Galo's voice?

01:18:29.350 --> 01:18:31.560
What's he doing?

01:18:31.810 --> 01:18:32.970
What's that robot?

01:18:33.430 --> 01:18:36.600
Where did he get it from?
Who made it?

01:18:36.940 --> 01:18:39.650
What the hell is going on, Galo!?

01:18:43.820 --> 01:18:46.280
Can you hear me, Heris?
It's me, Aina.

01:18:46.610 --> 01:18:48.320
Aina! Where have you been?

01:18:48.570 --> 01:18:51.490
<i>I'm OK.
More importantly, look at this.</i>

01:18:51.830 --> 01:18:54.500
<i>If you start the Prometech engine,</i>

01:18:54.500 --> 01:18:56.290
<i>the Earth's core'll go out of control.</i>

01:18:56.410 --> 01:18:58.120
You mustn't fly that ship!

01:18:58.450 --> 01:18:59.500
<i>Prof. Deus!</i>

01:18:59.500 --> 01:19:01.380
<i>The governor killed him?</i>

01:19:02.300 --> 01:19:03.710
This is...

01:19:04.550 --> 01:19:07.430
<i>It's fake footage,
made up by the rebels.</i>

01:19:07.430 --> 01:19:09.390
<i>Don't let it get to you.</i>

01:19:10.760 --> 01:19:14.720
Is it true?
Did Kray really kill Prof. Deus?

01:19:14.850 --> 01:19:17.190
<i>No doubt.
Deus told me personally.</i>

01:19:17.190 --> 01:19:19.560
<i>Anyway, Kray's engine is incomplete.</i>

01:19:19.560 --> 01:19:22.730
<i>If it takes off, the Earth'll...</i>

01:19:23.820 --> 01:19:25.690
Aina? Aina!

01:19:26.070 --> 01:19:28.740
<i>You cut off external communications.</i>

01:19:29.200 --> 01:19:30.410
It wasn't me.

01:19:30.410 --> 01:19:33.660
It's because of that robot's attack.

01:19:39.960 --> 01:19:43.040
Kick! Kick kick kick!

01:19:43.170 --> 01:19:46.010
Captured Burnish! Where are you?

01:19:46.420 --> 01:19:47.970
We're coming for you!

01:19:48.170 --> 01:19:50.300
Don't mind the small fry, Heris.

01:19:50.300 --> 01:19:53.140
Engine to full power.
We'll warp at once.

01:19:53.310 --> 01:19:54.930
<i>You don't care about the Earth?</i>

01:19:55.270 --> 01:19:57.980
Sooner or later, it'll be destroyed.

01:19:57.980 --> 01:20:00.440
Concentrate on the migration project.

01:20:00.650 --> 01:20:03.480
<i>You knew, didn't you?</i>

01:20:03.480 --> 01:20:06.360
<i>That using the engine 
would cause the planet's destruction.</i>

01:20:06.820 --> 01:20:09.610
It's either now or in six months.

01:20:10.700 --> 01:20:12.910
<i>Right. I got it.</i>

01:20:14.660 --> 01:20:18.040
Prometech engine, full power.

01:20:27.010 --> 01:20:28.880
<i>Oh no! They're about to warp!</i>

01:20:29.010 --> 01:20:30.510
Darn!

01:20:35.060 --> 01:20:38.060
Tell me! Where are the Burnish?

01:20:38.390 --> 01:20:41.560
<i>We can't go head. They'll smash the bridge.</i>

01:20:43.400 --> 01:20:45.900
All personnel move to the second bridge.

01:20:45.900 --> 01:20:49.740
Transfer the ship's main system 
to the second bridge.

01:20:51.200 --> 01:20:53.410
I'll get rid of that.

01:20:53.410 --> 01:20:56.280
Biar, you lead takeoff procedures.

01:20:56.530 --> 01:20:57.290
Yes, sir.

01:21:01.920 --> 01:21:04.830
Damn Galo.
Don't push your luck.

01:21:09.840 --> 01:21:11.380
What's that?

01:21:11.510 --> 01:21:13.430
Your futile struggle...

01:21:14.430 --> 01:21:17.890
is over!

01:21:31.150 --> 01:21:33.320
This voice... It's Kray.

01:21:33.910 --> 01:21:36.660
Free the Burnish, Kray!

01:21:37.120 --> 01:21:39.790
Filthy terrorists.
How dare you?

01:21:40.040 --> 01:21:41.290
Take this!

01:21:53.880 --> 01:21:54.220
What?

01:21:54.680 --> 01:21:56.720
The buildings turned into dirt!

01:21:57.180 --> 01:21:59.100
Genocide Cultivation Beam.

01:21:59.100 --> 01:22:02.560
Destroys mountains turning them into farmland.

01:22:02.560 --> 01:22:05.850
One of the terraforming tools 
we'll use on our new planet.

01:22:06.060 --> 01:22:08.690
I wasn't expecting to use it here.

01:22:08.820 --> 01:22:10.730
And the people inside?

01:22:10.730 --> 01:22:13.240
They're all in underground shelters, obviously.

01:22:17.160 --> 01:22:18.910
Damn you!

01:22:20.080 --> 01:22:24.160
Why don't you use your science
to bring the magma under control?

01:22:24.290 --> 01:22:27.170
I can't. That's why we're migrating.

01:22:27.170 --> 01:22:28.880
Do you want to destroy mankind so badly?

01:22:31.710 --> 01:22:33.800
If you know it's gonna be destroyed,

01:22:33.800 --> 01:22:35.090
you just have to stop it.

01:22:35.470 --> 01:22:38.850
And think about the rest later.

01:22:39.010 --> 01:22:41.970
You hopeless fool.

01:23:16.840 --> 01:23:19.970
I won't let you commit any more attrocities.

01:23:20.390 --> 01:23:24.770
Our Lio De Galon, or your Krazor X!

01:23:26.600 --> 01:23:29.730
Let's see which is more powerful!

01:23:29.900 --> 01:23:30.230
Lio!

01:23:30.730 --> 01:23:31.360
OK.

01:23:51.630 --> 01:23:54.130
You stopped Lio De Galon's flames.

01:23:54.130 --> 01:23:56.420
True to your name, Krazor X.

01:23:56.800 --> 01:23:57.800
But...

01:24:01.640 --> 01:24:05.220
Take this, Krazor X!

01:24:09.640 --> 01:24:10.730
You...

01:24:11.980 --> 01:24:14.230
and your...

01:24:14.690 --> 01:24:18.490
stupid names!

01:24:23.320 --> 01:24:25.490
Pulverizing Pile Driver.

01:24:25.490 --> 01:24:29.080
Designed to break 
through hard bedrock to reach water veins.

01:24:29.580 --> 01:24:33.750
Against this, your armor's paper!

01:24:52.600 --> 01:24:53.900
That robot's bad news!

01:24:54.150 --> 01:24:57.070
We can't win like this.

01:24:57.070 --> 01:24:59.740
I wish I had my matoi gear.

01:25:00.030 --> 01:25:00.700
Matoi?

01:25:01.780 --> 01:25:03.620
That weird decoration you wore?

01:25:03.740 --> 01:25:04.910
It's not weird!

01:25:04.910 --> 01:25:08.330
It embodies the heritage
 of a Far East island's firefighter.

01:25:08.540 --> 01:25:09.540
Right.

01:25:25.680 --> 01:25:26.470
Like this?

01:25:30.520 --> 01:25:32.190
Awesome!

01:25:36.520 --> 01:25:41.150
Matoi really fires me up!

01:25:46.660 --> 01:25:51.560
Gaze in awe!
Lio De Galon Matoi Decked Out!

01:25:54.790 --> 01:25:55.580
What?

01:26:00.090 --> 01:26:01.010
Heris!

01:26:04.430 --> 01:26:05.010
Doctor!

01:26:05.010 --> 01:26:08.300
The engine's out of control due to overfueling.

01:26:08.300 --> 01:26:12.680
At this rate, the central pod will
 overheat and explode!

01:26:32.410 --> 01:26:34.120
<i>Heris, what happened?</i>

01:26:34.750 --> 01:26:38.920
I've destroyed the central pod 
by overloading it with energy.

01:26:39.130 --> 01:26:41.000
The engine won't work anymore.

01:26:41.300 --> 01:26:42.710
<i>You did it intentionally!</i>

01:26:43.130 --> 01:26:45.760
I was wrong to trust you.

01:26:47.470 --> 01:26:52.060
That idiot. She's been blinded by her love for her sister.

01:26:52.680 --> 01:26:54.230
Call Colonel Vulcan!

01:26:56.520 --> 01:26:58.190
Ouch.

01:26:58.310 --> 01:27:00.190
Looks like the ship's crashed.

01:27:00.400 --> 01:27:02.320
The warp gate must have closed.

01:27:05.700 --> 01:27:08.410
We can no longer stop Earth's destruction.

01:27:08.530 --> 01:27:11.910
This ship and its passengers 
are the only future for mankind.

01:27:12.580 --> 01:27:17.040
And it's Kray Foresight 
who'll create that future!

01:27:27.760 --> 01:27:30.250
Absolute Zero Heat Death Cannon.

01:27:30.250 --> 01:27:33.600
The ultimate freezing weapon,
created for protection

01:27:33.600 --> 01:27:37.390
from Promare attacks and 
solar flares on the new planet.

01:27:38.100 --> 01:27:41.270
Why don't you use that to save the Earth then?

01:27:41.400 --> 01:27:43.940
You must reach the core for that.

01:27:44.820 --> 01:27:48.450
This machine will not withstand that.

01:27:48.450 --> 01:27:49.990
You just want to migrate no matter what.

01:27:49.990 --> 01:27:53.120
Cool that hard head of yours instead!

01:27:53.490 --> 01:27:57.210
Do you think two fools like you can beat me?

01:27:57.660 --> 01:28:02.000
Go to absolute zero freezing hell!

01:28:03.000 --> 01:28:05.510
Galo, you didn't even try to avoid it.

01:28:05.510 --> 01:28:07.010
What's your strategy?

01:28:07.010 --> 01:28:09.630
Grinning and bearing it!
That's my strategy!

01:28:09.680 --> 01:28:11.390
Are you an idiot?

01:28:12.260 --> 01:28:15.770
Yeah.
The world's #1 firefighting idiot!

01:28:16.310 --> 01:28:18.230
I'll put 'em out now.

01:28:18.230 --> 01:28:21.480
Both your flames and your stupid ambitions!

01:28:21.690 --> 01:28:24.150
All right!

01:28:24.270 --> 01:28:28.990
Try it if you can!

01:28:51.760 --> 01:28:52.800
Did we beat him?

01:28:52.970 --> 01:28:55.140
Wait. Look.

01:28:56.060 --> 01:28:59.700
Do you want to save your brothers that much, Lio Fotia?

01:28:59.700 --> 01:29:04.810
But you can't.
The Burnish are destined to die.

01:29:05.730 --> 01:29:09.600
Listen to their death throes.

01:29:14.410 --> 01:29:15.150
Kray!

01:29:15.450 --> 01:29:19.100
If you hate me, attack me.
Fire-spitting fool...

01:29:19.100 --> 01:29:20.540
Lio Fotia!

01:29:20.660 --> 01:29:22.330
I'll never...

01:29:24.330 --> 01:29:27.710
Stop it. Calm down, Lio!
Stop! Don't kill him.

01:29:29.710 --> 01:29:30.800
I'll never...

01:29:32.510 --> 01:29:33.630
forgive you!

01:29:39.810 --> 01:29:45.350
Do you think you can burn me
with those pathetic flames?

01:29:46.150 --> 01:29:49.480
You Burnish are just a bunch of fools.

01:29:49.610 --> 01:29:50.230
What?

01:29:50.480 --> 01:29:51.940
Don't tell me you...

01:29:52.280 --> 01:29:54.240
Indeed.

01:29:54.700 --> 01:29:59.410
I have the same ugly mutation.
That's why I understand...

01:29:59.830 --> 01:30:03.620
how hard it is to have
a strong enough will

01:30:03.620 --> 01:30:06.540
to control the flames
and fight the urge

01:30:06.540 --> 01:30:09.550
to burn everything
to the ground.

01:30:09.590 --> 01:30:12.720
The Burnish are controlled by the Promare.

01:30:12.720 --> 01:30:16.430
They're slaves to their instincts.

01:30:16.840 --> 01:30:18.930
You make it sound like you're different.

01:30:19.100 --> 01:30:22.220
Because that's the truth.

01:30:23.310 --> 01:30:24.440
You can't move.

01:30:24.640 --> 01:30:27.980
My Burnish power's stronger than yours.

01:30:28.110 --> 01:30:28.770
Darn.

01:30:28.900 --> 01:30:34.280
But, your power's enough
to restart the Prometech engine.

01:30:34.280 --> 01:30:36.410
You'll be the engine's core.

01:30:36.490 --> 01:30:37.200
What?

01:30:37.320 --> 01:30:39.200
Thank you.

01:30:41.740 --> 01:30:43.200
Let Lio go, Kray!

01:30:43.830 --> 01:30:44.910
Good grief.

01:30:49.840 --> 01:30:53.630
You've been an eyesore
 from the moment I met you.

01:30:53.840 --> 01:30:57.340
<i>I had the first Burnish spasm
 when I was a student.</i>

01:30:57.680 --> 01:31:01.250
<i>I was trying to hold back the flames, but I couldn't.</i>

01:31:01.560 --> 01:31:04.270
So, you didn't save me?

01:31:05.560 --> 01:31:08.900
<i>No, I took care of you by chance.</i>

01:31:08.900 --> 01:31:12.400
<i>It was a good opportunity
 to build my reputation.</i>

01:31:12.900 --> 01:31:13.860
No...

01:31:14.400 --> 01:31:16.860
<i>I made you a Burning Rescue
member because it was</i>

01:31:16.860 --> 01:31:19.450
<i>the job with the highest mortality rate.</i>

01:31:19.820 --> 01:31:22.200
<i>I wanted you to disappear, but you kept</i>

01:31:22.200 --> 01:31:24.950
<i>coming back even after getting injured.</i>

01:31:25.290 --> 01:31:28.080
<i>My life's always gone as planned.</i>

01:31:28.080 --> 01:31:31.000
<i>But you constantly mess up my plans.</i>

01:31:31.500 --> 01:31:33.880
You're really an eyesore of an idiot!

01:31:34.670 --> 01:31:36.340
Kray, you bastard.

01:31:36.840 --> 01:31:39.220
But this is the end for you, fool.

01:31:39.390 --> 01:31:40.390
Galo!

01:31:52.820 --> 01:31:53.730
You monster!

01:31:54.190 --> 01:31:55.480
No...

01:31:57.280 --> 01:31:59.860
A savior!

01:32:00.660 --> 01:32:02.990
Savior of mankind!

01:32:21.300 --> 01:32:23.510
You can't run away.

01:32:25.650 --> 01:32:31.310
It was foolish of you
to go against the governor.

01:32:37.030 --> 01:32:39.650
She chose to die.

01:32:42.200 --> 01:32:43.570
What?

01:32:44.160 --> 01:32:45.530
Cheeky bastards!

01:32:51.170 --> 01:32:51.540
Aina!

01:32:51.710 --> 01:32:54.710
We made it. 
I'll go get Galo!

01:33:01.050 --> 01:33:03.140
Galo!

01:33:05.680 --> 01:33:09.890
Your brothers are inside the surrounding pods.

01:33:09.890 --> 01:33:12.310
You'll fly us all over the stars,

01:33:12.310 --> 01:33:14.940
shouldering your fellow's screams.

01:33:14.940 --> 01:33:18.030
And you'll become the myth of mankind.

01:33:18.030 --> 01:33:21.240
An undue luxury for a Burnish fool.

01:33:21.360 --> 01:33:23.200
You won't get away with this.

01:33:27.200 --> 01:33:29.080
Come on, get angry.

01:33:29.910 --> 01:33:34.580
Your rage will power the engine.

01:33:35.400 --> 01:33:39.590
This is Kray. Restart countdown.
We'll warp in five minutes.

01:33:39.960 --> 01:33:40.880
Roger.

01:33:41.880 --> 01:33:44.510
Parnassus, five minutes to warp.

01:33:46.050 --> 01:33:47.760
Galo! Galo!

01:33:47.890 --> 01:33:49.680
He's still on fire.

01:33:50.810 --> 01:33:51.430
Wait!

01:33:59.280 --> 01:34:00.440
Are you OK, Galo?

01:34:00.480 --> 01:34:02.150
Yeah.

01:34:03.400 --> 01:34:04.950
Lio protected me.

01:34:08.780 --> 01:34:10.490
The ship's gonna warp!

01:34:10.580 --> 01:34:12.830
How?
I destroyed the engine.

01:34:12.960 --> 01:34:15.080
He said he'll use Lio as the engine's core.

01:34:15.250 --> 01:34:16.630
Doctor, where's the engine?

01:34:16.830 --> 01:34:17.670
What's the plan?

01:34:18.000 --> 01:34:20.130
I'll go save Lio.

01:34:20.250 --> 01:34:24.550
How? I know you're going to say
you'll just crash into the core.

01:34:25.180 --> 01:34:27.850
Yeah, I'm a Burning Rescue member.

01:34:27.850 --> 01:34:29.510
Rescue and firefighting's my job.

01:34:30.060 --> 01:34:31.970
I'll save Lio and put out...

01:34:34.310 --> 01:34:35.810
Ignis!

01:34:35.810 --> 01:34:38.310
Hand over the doctor and that punk.

01:34:38.310 --> 01:34:40.400
Or you'll be treated as traitors too.

01:34:40.520 --> 01:34:41.150
I refuse.

01:34:41.400 --> 01:34:44.450
You've got some guts defying Freeze Force.

01:34:44.820 --> 01:34:47.870
It's an emergency.
I've authorized them to fight.

01:34:48.410 --> 01:34:50.700
All of you'll be purged anyway.

01:34:50.910 --> 01:34:52.620
I refuse.

01:34:52.950 --> 01:34:53.580
Firm refusal.

01:34:53.910 --> 01:34:54.410
Lucia!

01:34:54.960 --> 01:34:55.500
OK.

01:34:58.420 --> 01:35:03.170
<i>I put new drill gear 
on the spare Matoi just in case.</i>

01:35:03.170 --> 01:35:04.420
<i>You never know.</i>

01:35:04.720 --> 01:35:05.720
<i>What? A drill?</i>

01:35:05.800 --> 01:35:07.930
Yup, the ultimate in armor-piercing tech.

01:35:08.260 --> 01:35:10.600
I sent you the ship's data.

01:35:11.060 --> 01:35:14.310
<i>I'll calculate the angle and 
send you straight to the engine.</i>

01:35:14.480 --> 01:35:15.640
I appreciate it.

01:35:17.060 --> 01:35:19.610
<i>No time to announce
 yourself. Just go!</i>

01:35:19.770 --> 01:35:20.400
<i>Go!</i>

01:35:29.780 --> 01:35:32.830
I'm coming, Lio!

01:35:40.040 --> 01:35:40.880
This is...

01:36:00.060 --> 01:36:01.270
Vulcan!

01:36:01.400 --> 01:36:02.860
Ignis!

01:36:10.160 --> 01:36:12.450
How long must this go on?

01:36:12.570 --> 01:36:14.790
There's no time left, methinks.

01:36:15.240 --> 01:36:16.660
Promare activity has increased.

01:36:17.250 --> 01:36:17.910
Galo...

01:37:01.790 --> 01:37:02.670
Lio!

01:37:03.000 --> 01:37:04.210
Are you OK, Lio?

01:37:06.960 --> 01:37:07.670
Oh no!

01:37:14.760 --> 01:37:17.640
Are you still alive?
You're so annoying.

01:37:17.770 --> 01:37:20.310
Don't mess with rescue operations. Back off!

01:37:20.350 --> 01:37:22.140
I'll extinguish you.

01:37:22.230 --> 01:37:25.810
Extinguishing is <i>my</i> job!

01:37:28.780 --> 01:37:31.650
Your struggle's useless!

01:37:40.580 --> 01:37:41.870
What?!

01:38:07.770 --> 01:38:12.740
It's the same as before.
 Lio's fire protected me.

01:38:12.990 --> 01:38:15.070
This shielded me from your flames.

01:38:16.570 --> 01:38:21.410
I'll save him. And the Earth. And you too.

01:38:21.790 --> 01:38:23.120
Me?

01:38:32.010 --> 01:38:33.470
Shut up and watch.

01:38:38.010 --> 01:38:39.850
Hey! Don't die!

01:38:40.140 --> 01:38:42.020
Lio! Lio!

01:38:43.480 --> 01:38:45.690
Damn! Don't disappear!

01:38:47.650 --> 01:38:49.820
All right, I've got no choice.

01:39:25.230 --> 01:39:26.980
Galo...?

01:39:28.310 --> 01:39:30.440
You made it, Lio.

01:39:31.440 --> 01:39:33.980
Did you save me?

01:39:37.990 --> 01:39:40.820
Darn! For the first time in my life...

01:39:40.820 --> 01:39:42.830
I lit a fire, because of you!

01:39:42.830 --> 01:39:46.040
What are you going 
to do about this? You jerk!

01:39:47.370 --> 01:39:50.330
Then let's just burn
 the Earth to the ground.

01:39:52.000 --> 01:39:54.760
Inside the pod,
 I synched with the Promare

01:39:54.760 --> 01:39:56.220
in the core and now I know.

01:39:56.760 --> 01:39:59.180
Their combustion's incomplete.

01:39:59.180 --> 01:40:01.180
We need to let them burn completely once.

01:40:01.350 --> 01:40:05.180
You can't tell a firefighter to do that, you idiot.

01:40:05.270 --> 01:40:08.560
We need your firefighter's soul.

01:40:08.560 --> 01:40:10.150
Let's use it once again.

01:40:10.440 --> 01:40:13.150
But, this time it'll be Galo De Lion.

01:40:16.860 --> 01:40:19.030
Wait, what are you doing?

01:40:19.490 --> 01:40:22.120
Going firefighting, of course.

01:40:22.120 --> 01:40:25.290
We'll put out the core's fire and your ambitions.

01:40:29.080 --> 01:40:31.540
We need all the Burnish's help too.

01:40:31.540 --> 01:40:34.420
Our flames'll burn the whole planet!

01:40:35.050 --> 01:40:35.960
OK, Boss!

01:40:36.340 --> 01:40:38.300
Let's do it, Boss!

01:40:38.850 --> 01:40:42.100
Boss!

01:40:45.140 --> 01:40:49.560
I'll show you
 my burning firefighter's soul!

01:40:50.060 --> 01:40:50.850
What?

01:41:13.330 --> 01:41:15.340
Oh no! Oh no! I'm burning!

01:41:15.790 --> 01:41:18.130
Darn Galo,
he didn't make it in time?

01:41:18.420 --> 01:41:20.220
But, these flames...

01:41:20.300 --> 01:41:21.840
Yeah, that's right.

01:41:22.380 --> 01:41:23.700
They're not hot.

01:41:23.700 --> 01:41:26.470
It's the same as Galo earlier.
They're protecting us.

01:41:35.520 --> 01:41:39.350
Yes. The Promare synch with the humans' will.

01:41:39.350 --> 01:41:42.360
When my urge to burn everything...

01:41:42.800 --> 01:41:47.000
and my will to save lives from fire...

01:41:47.000 --> 01:41:50.100
join as one...

01:42:29.400 --> 01:42:32.800
...our flames'll burn out the Earth.

01:42:32.800 --> 01:42:36.450
Complete combustion of the whole planet...

01:42:36.750 --> 01:42:41.600
I'll put you out with my burning soul!

01:44:04.960 --> 01:44:06.010
What did you do?

01:44:06.760 --> 01:44:09.970
We satisfied the Promare's primal drive to burn,

01:44:09.970 --> 01:44:11.850
sent them back to their universe,

01:44:11.850 --> 01:44:13.720
and closed the dimensional rupture.

01:44:14.930 --> 01:44:18.940
There are no Promare nor Burnish
 in this world anymore.

01:44:21.230 --> 01:44:22.700
That was uncalled for.

01:44:29.200 --> 01:44:33.240
It burned like a dream!

01:44:33.780 --> 01:44:35.080
This is the beginning.

01:44:37.250 --> 01:44:39.120
This city's new beginning.

01:44:39.920 --> 01:44:44.210
Let's clean up after the fire.
Lio, you're gonna help too.

01:44:44.420 --> 01:44:45.090
What?

01:44:45.210 --> 01:44:46.760
We're short of hands.

01:44:46.760 --> 01:44:49.130
We'll get your buddies to help too.

01:44:49.260 --> 01:44:50.050
But...

01:44:50.220 --> 01:44:54.100
Don't worry. If the haters give
you heat, I'll put 'em out.

01:44:54.100 --> 01:44:57.000
Through spark and flame,
I got your back.

01:44:59.300 --> 01:45:01.850
You really are an idiot.

01:45:01.850 --> 01:45:02.800
Yeah.

01:45:02.800 --> 01:45:07.350
The universe's #1 firefighting idiot!
